{
  "summary": "Replaces the bespoke network name parser in `-proxy` argument handling with the shared `ParseNetwork()` function, preserving original user casing in startup error diagnostics. Updates the `-proxy` CLI help string and `doc/tor.md` to reference `onion` instead of the obsolete `tor` network identifier removed in #34031. Adds functional tests for legacy and unsupported network names across `-proxy`, `-onlynet`, and `getnodeaddresses`.",
  "problem": "PR #34031 removed `tor` as an accepted network name, but documentation in `doc/tor.md` and CLI help for `-proxy` still instructed users to use `=tor`. Following official examples causes Bitcoin Core to exit with an unrecognized network error on startup.",
  "evidence": [
